                                "title": "Aquaculture production (encouragement of aquaculture, establishment of hatchery, rehabilitation of breeding plants, collection and import).",
                                "description": "<p>1. Domestic aquaculture products are increasing steadily, so there is a need to reduce imports to allow domestic aquaculture products to enter the market. Surplus supply causes the price of aquaculture products to fall, resulting in low profits for the domestic aquaculturists.<br>2. Imports of fish from neighboring countries are in large quantities and of poor quality, affecting domestic prices and the well-being of citizens.</p>",
